  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A. NEW - ELISSA Phase 3 (2025 - 2026)
&#xa0;
Description:&#xa0;

ELISSA Phase 3 will be a continuation of the Enhancing Livelihoods in Sub Sahara Africa (ELISSA project), designed for a subsequent 3 years to grow on the learning and successes in the previous phase.&#xa0;&#xa0;
&#xa0;


ELISSA Phase 3 will aim to build resilience among the most vulnerable 8 communities in 3 Constituencies in the Shiselweni Region by targeting 5853 HH, 39,818 people which will include women and children with diversified livelihoods interventions by 2028.&#xa0;

&#xa0;

The intervention aims at promoting climate-smart agriculture, improving market access, and fostering community-led nutrition practices, ensuring long term-term food security, while empowering communities through skills development and sustainable agricultural practices. The Red Cross branch and implementation team will play a critical role at all stages of the project life cycle, including community engagement and accountability. 
&#xa0;
Please note that the revised budget only includes the additional funding for Y1 of Phase 3, the budget for subsequent years will be added once confirmed. 

&#xa0;
Phase 2 Description - 2022 to 2025
&#xa0;
&#xa0;
Objective - Phase 2
Communities in Silele have improved nutritional outcomes and are able to adapt their livelihood options to a changing climate.
&#xa0;
&#xa0;
ELISSA Phase 2
-Year 1 [2022/2023] Actual Grant:&#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; GBP 185,018
-Year 2&amp;3 [2023/2025] Actual Grant: GBP 387,993
* Total Grant Phase 1: GBP 573,011
&#xa0;
ELISSA Phase 3
-Year 1&#xa0;[2025/2026] Actual Grant: GBP 205,000
-Year 2&amp;3 a decision was made to combine ELISSA Phase 3 Years 2&amp;3 with DM.
&#xa0;
ELISSA TOTAL GRANT: GBP 778,011
&#xa0;
********************************************************************************************
&#xa0;
B. Baphalali Eswatini Climate Resilience Project (BECRP) - (Combined ELISSA, CVA and DM) - [Apr 2026 - Mar 2028]

&#xa0;
The Baphalali Eswatini Climate Resilience Project (BECRP) is a unified, multi&#x2011;year initiative implemented jointly by the Baphalali Eswatini Red Cross Society (BERCS) and the British Red Cross (BRC). It brings together three previously separate efforts&#x2014;ELISSA Phase III, the Disaster Management Community Resilience project, and Cash and Voucher Assistance preparedness&#x2014;into one strategically coordinated resilience programme. This integration enables BERCS to deliver a comprehensive package of activities in health, livelihoods, disaster risk reduction, environmental management, and institutional strengthening across the Shiselweni and Lubombo regions, as well as at the national level.
&#xa0;


BECRP Proposed Amount GBP 345,000 [Apr 2026 - Mar 2027]
&#xa0;
Allocated Budget
a. ELISSA Intervention:&#xa0; GBP 778,011
b. Eswatini Climate Resilience: GBP 345,000
TOTAL Grant ELISSA &amp; ECRP: GBP1,123,011</narrative>
